 it would turn into a song  there's one line in  in the song and it says that the wii  is now you  and i was talking about me the wii and  linda it's now you because  you take care of me  you do everything for me i can't dole  out my own medications  [Music]  after months of rehearsing with  therapist becky wellman jim sang his  gift to linda on her birthday words of  love and gratitude for her sacrifices  strength and commitment truly from his  heart this was just the man that i  married  46 years ago that really had that kind  of caring compassion that  i know it's in there but i don't always  see it and it was nice to see it it was  nice to have him back for that amount of  time it was nice for me too by the way  [Laughter]  it was really a sweet story well if  you're a caregiver and you're looking  for support you can connect with the lou  rouveaux center for brain health or the  alzheimer's association we'll have those  links on our website i'm not going to  lie i shed a tear or two oh for sure of  course when i saw that and i talked to  them and you know  jim was having a really good day that  day and he was very lucid and he was  talking and it and that's the thing a  lot of times with dementia especially  louis body dementia and my mom had louis  body dementia  there are days where you would talk with  that person you go i don't see  that they have an issue at all or a  problem and then there are other days  when you're living with them day in and  day out like linda does  it can get very stressful and very  trying and that's the part of caregiving  that most people don't see  and that's where the strength and the  sacrifices come in and why it's so  important to support those who are  caregivers in the community because it's  a day-to-day  caregiving is a day-to-day thing and to  honor what they do and respect what they  do and support what they do because  it becomes routine  you have to acknowledge the fact that  the routine is unusual but it's so  important and it can be very isolating  please if you have friends that are  going through this don't leave them  alone reach out be there for them  absolutely
 

